{
  "schema_version": "argument_graph/0.1",
  "example_id": "persuade:97DD2D770B03",
  "root": "u3",
  "units": [
    {
      "id": "u1",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 17,
      "text": "Dear Mr. Senator,",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "unclear",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u2",
      "start": 19,
      "end": 146,
      "text": "I have decided to express my opinon to you about the Electoral College process for electing the President of the United States.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u3",
      "start": 147,
      "end": 199,
      "text": "This process should be abolished as soon as possible",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u4",
      "start": 200,
      "end": 251,
      "text": "for it is corrosive to the American peoples opinon.",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u5",
      "start": 252,
      "end": 345,
      "text": "We should instead switch to a popular vote by eligble American citizens to decide presidency.",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u6",
      "start": 347,
      "end": 375,
      "text": "Now some fellows might argue",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u7",
      "start": 376,
      "end": 428,
      "text": "that the Electoral College is favored by the people.",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "rejected",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u8",
      "start": 429,
      "end": 488,
      "text": "When in fact, as Bradford Plumer points out in paragraph 9,",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u9",
      "start": 489,
      "end": 567,
      "text": "\"60 percent of voters would prefer a direct election to the kind we have now\".",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u10",
      "start": 568,
      "end": 592,
      "text": "Some people may also say",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u11",
      "start": 593,
      "end": 664,
      "text": "that the Electoral college ecourages the president to visit all states,",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "rejected",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u12",
      "start": 665,
      "end": 760,
      "text": "when in fact smaller states still are not treated the same as states with more electoral votes.",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u13",
      "start": 761,
      "end": 1065,
      "text": "A president would rather spend their time investing and giving information to a state such as Californa who have 55 electoral votes, who feel more inclined to think about their decision due to their involvement, rather than a state with 3 electoral votes who dont invest as much thought into their votes.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u14",
      "start": 1067,
      "end": 1096,
      "text": "In grade school we are taught",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u15",
      "start": 1097,
      "end": 1176,
      "text": "that popualer votes most accurately represent what a specific population wants,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u16",
      "start": 1177,
      "end": 1214,
      "text": "why dont we use it in the real world?",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u17",
      "start": 1215,
      "end": 1301,
      "text": "If your princible wanted to figure out what color the students wanted their yearbooks,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u18",
      "start": 1302,
      "end": 1354,
      "text": "she would not elect people to decide for each class!",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u19",
      "start": 1355,
      "end": 1432,
      "text": "In the Bush and Gore election, Bush recived less votes by the American people",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u20",
      "start": 1433,
      "end": 1451,
      "text": "but won presidency",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u21",
      "start": 1452,
      "end": 1503,
      "text": "because he accuired more Electoral votes than Gore.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u22",
      "start": 1504,
      "end": 1553,
      "text": "That means that more American people wanted Gore,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u23",
      "start": 1554,
      "end": 1625,
      "text": "but the fate was chosen by 271 people, who selected Bush as the winner!",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u24",
      "start": 1627,
      "end": 1681,
      "text": "The Electoral College also increases the risk of a tie",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u25",
      "start": 1682,
      "end": 1701,
      "text": "and if one occured,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u26",
      "start": 1702,
      "end": 1814,
      "text": "the election would be disrupted by the unorderly process of which we would have to take to decide the president.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u27",
      "start": 1815,
      "end": 1941,
      "text": "In 1968, a change of votes from just 41,971 people would have tied the electoral votes due to the even number of 538 Electors.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u28",
      "start": 1943,
      "end": 2048,
      "text": "The overall idea im trying to express is that the Electoral College is a poor way to show peoples opinon,",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u29",
      "start": 2049,
      "end": 2158,
      "text": "and much rather focuses on that of 270 individuals who in the end, decide the President of the United States.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u30",
      "start": 2159,
      "end": 2187,
      "text": "I hope you can see my points",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u31",
      "start": 2188,
      "end": 2255,
      "text": "and I long for the day when the president is decided by the people.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    }
  ],
